# Web routes and servers (D51) belong to `otter serve`; `otter run` parses
# them and stops when one runs. `await` (D56) is not part of Otter 1.0.
to fetchThing
    return 5
.
try
    when api receives GET at "/hello" into request
        respond with "hi"
    .
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    when api receives a request at "/any"
        respond with status 404
    .
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    respond with "x" as json and status 201
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    respond with status 500
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    start api
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    start the api
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    listen on port 8080
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    listen port 8080
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    listen api
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    await fetchThing
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    await get "http://example.test"
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    say await fetchThing
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
try
    value is await 5 plus 1
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
say "done"
